---
import ToolPage from '../../../layouts/ToolPage.astro';

const steps = [
  'Drop in a screen recording: MP4, WebM or MOV. A Mac recording (Cmd + Shift + 5) or a Loom or OBS download all work. No recording at hand? Try the sample.',
  'Drag the two handles on the strip under the video to keep just the part you want. Pick a width, a frame rate, a speed and whether it loops.',
  'Watch the GIF and its size update as you go. When it says it fits where you’re posting, download it, or copy the Markdown for your README.',
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'Is my video uploaded anywhere?', a: 'No. Your browser reads the video and makes the GIF on your own computer. Nothing is sent to us or anyone else.' },
  { q: 'How big can a GIF be?', a: 'GitHub takes images up to <strong>10 MB</strong> in READMEs, issues and pull requests. Discord’s free limit is also <strong>10 MB</strong>. X takes GIFs up to <strong>15 MB</strong>. The tool shows a green tick or a red cross for each as soon as your GIF is ready.' },
  { q: 'My GIF is too big. What should I change first?', a: 'In this order: make the clip shorter, then pick a smaller width (480 is still readable for most screen recordings), then a lower frame rate (10 fps is fine for clicking around an app). Or press <strong>Make it smaller</strong> and the tool steps them down for you. Speeding the clip up to 1.5× also helps, because there are fewer frames.' },
  { q: 'Why is a GIF so much bigger than my video?', a: 'GIF is a format from 1987. It stores every frame as a picture with at most 256 colors, with no clever video compression. That’s why the tool can also make an MP4 or WebM of the same clip, often 5 to 20 times smaller. GitHub plays MP4 and WebM files you drag into an issue, a pull request or a README you edit on github.com.' },
  { q: 'Why do some colors look a bit grainy?', a: 'A GIF can only use 256 colors per frame. Flat app screens look fine; photos, gradients and shadows can look grainy. If that matters, use the MP4 instead.' },
  { q: 'What’s the Markdown for my README?', a: 'Put the GIF in your repo (for example in a <code>docs/</code> folder) and add <code>![Demo](docs/demo.gif)</code> to your README. The <strong>Copy Markdown</strong> button gives you that line with your file’s name.' },
];
---
<ToolPage
  slug="video-to-gif"
  title="Free video to GIF converter for screen recordings · Darnly"
  description="Turn a screen recording (MP4, WebM or MOV) into a GIF. Trim it, pick the width and frame rate, and see the size live, with a check for GitHub and X limits. Free, and nothing is uploaded."
  h1="Video to GIF: turn a screen recording into a GIF"
  lede="Drop in a screen recording, trim it, and get a GIF for your README, bug report or post. You see the GIF and its size as you change things, and whether it fits on GitHub and X. It runs in your browser, so nothing is uploaded."
  steps={steps}
  faq={faq}
>
  <div class="vg">
    <div class="start" id="vg-start">
      <label class="drop" id="vg-drop">
        <input id="vg-file" type="file" accept="video/*,.mov,.mkv" />
        <strong>Drop your screen recording here</strong>
        <span>or click to choose a file. MP4, WebM or MOV.</span>
      </label>
      <button id="vg-sample" type="button" class="link">No video at hand? Try it with a sample recording</button>
    </div>
    <p class="error" id="vg-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

    <div class="work" id="vg-work" hidden>
      <div class="panes">
        <section class="pane" aria-labelledby="vg-h-trim">
          <h2 class="pane-h" id="vg-h-trim"><span>1</span> Trim your video</h2>
          <div class="video-box">
            <video id="vg-video" muted playsinline></video>
          </div>
          <div class="tl" id="vg-tl">
            <canvas id="vg-strip" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
            <div class="shade" id="vg-shade-l"></div>
            <div class="shade" id="vg-shade-r"></div>
            <div class="sel" id="vg-sel"></div>
            <div class="playhead" id="vg-playhead"></div>
            <div class="handle" id="vg-h1" role="slider" tabindex="0" aria-label="Start of the GIF"></div>
            <div class="handle" id="vg-h2" role="slider" tabindex="0" aria-label="End of the GIF"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="trim" id="vg-trim"></p>

          <div class="controls">
            <label>Width
              <select id="vg-width"></select>
            </label>
            <label>Frame rate
              <select id="vg-fps">
                <option value="8">8 fps (smallest)</option>
                <option value="10">10 fps</option>
                <option value="12" selected>12 fps</option>
                <option value="15">15 fps</option>
                <option value="20">20 fps</option>
                <option value="25">25 fps (smoothest)</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>Speed
              <select id="vg-speed">
                <option value="1" selected>1×</option>
                <option value="1.5">1.5×</option>
                <option value="2">2×</option>
                <option value="3">3×</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>Loop
              <select id="vg-loop">
                <option value="0" selected>Forever</option>
                <option value="-1">Play once</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="pane" aria-labelledby="vg-h-gif">
          <h2 class="pane-h" id="vg-h-gif"><span>2</span> Your GIF</h2>
          <div class="gif-box">
            <img id="vg-gif" alt="Your GIF" hidden />
            <div class="busy" id="vg-busy" hidden>
              <div class="bar"><span id="vg-bar"></span></div>
              <p id="vg-busy-text">Making your GIF…</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="size">
            <strong id="vg-size">…</strong>
            <span id="vg-meta"></span>
          </div>
          <ul class="fits" id="vg-fits" aria-label="Where it fits"></ul>
          <p class="tip" id="vg-tip" hidden>
            <span id="vg-tip-text"></span>
            <button id="vg-smaller" type="button">Make it smaller</button>
          </p>
          <div class="buttons">
            <a id="vg-download" class="btn primary" download="demo.gif" aria-disabled="true">Download GIF</a>
            <button id="vg-md" type="button" class="btn ghost">Copy Markdown</button>
          </div>
          <div class="alt">
            <p><strong>Want it much smaller?</strong> The same clip as a video file is often 5 to 20 times smaller, and GitHub plays it too.</p>
            <div class="alt-row">
              <button id="vg-vid" type="button" class="btn ghost">Make a <span id="vg-vid-kind">video</span> instead</button>
              <span id="vg-vid-out" role="status"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="bug">Recording a bug for your AI agent? <a id="vg-darnly" href="/">Darnly</a> captures it in one click, with the page details your agent needs.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <button id="vg-reset" type="button" class="btn ghost reset">Use another video</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  import '../../../scripts/video-to-gif';
</script>

<style>
  .vg { display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  .start { display: grid; gap: 12px; justify-items: center; }
  .start[hidden], .work[hidden], .error[hidden], .tip[hidden], .busy[hidden], img[hidden] { display: none; }
  .drop { position: relative; display: grid; place-items: center; gap: 6px; text-align: center; padding: 56px 24px; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; border: 2px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--wash); cursor: pointer; }
  .drop:hover, .drop:global(.over) { border-color: var(--sky); }
  .drop input { position: absolute; inset: 0; opacity: 0; cursor: pointer; }
  .drop strong { font: 700 22px/1.2 var(--display); }
  .drop span { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .drop:focus-within { outline: 3px solid var(--pink); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .link { font: 600 16px/1.3 var(--body); color: var(--sky); background: none; border: 0; padding: 6px; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .link:disabled { color: var(--ink-soft); cursor: wait; text-decoration: none; }
  .error { margin: 0; color: #B4234F; }

  .work { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .panes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; align-items: start; }
  .pane { display: grid; gap: 14px; padding: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--white); min-width: 0; }
  .pane-h { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 0; font: 700 19px/1.2 var(--display); }
  .pane-h span { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ink); color: var(--white); font: 700 14px/1 var(--body); }

  .video-box, .gif-box { position: relative; display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 200px; border-radius: 12px; background: repeating-conic-gradient(#e6eef2 0 25%, #fff 0 50%) 0 0 / 16px 16px; overflow: hidden; }
  .video-box video { display: block; width: 100%; max-height: 360px; background: #0B2230; }
  .gif-box img { display: block; max-width: 100%; max-height: 360px; }
  .busy { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-content: center; gap: 10px; justify-items: center; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82); }
  .busy p { margin: 0; font-weight: 600; }
  .bar { width: 200px; height: 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--line); overflow: hidden; }
  .bar span { display: block; height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--sky); transition: width 0.15s; }

  .tl { position: relative; height: 56px; border-radius: 10px; background: #0B2230; touch-action: none; user-select: none; }
  .tl canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border-radius: 10px; }
  .shade { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; background: rgba(11, 34, 48, 0.7); pointer-events: none; }
  #vg-shade-l { left: 0; border-radius: 10px 0 0 10px; }
  #vg-shade-r { right: 0; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; }
  .sel { position: absolute; top: -3px; bottom: -3px; border: 3px solid #FFC83D; border-radius: 6px; cursor: grab; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .sel:active { cursor: grabbing; }
  .playhead { position: absolute; top: -6px; bottom: -6px; width: 2px; margin-left: -1px; background: var(--white); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); pointer-events: none; }
  .handle { position: absolute; top: -3px; bottom: -3px; width: 18px; margin-left: -9px; border-radius: 6px; background: #FFC83D; cursor: ew-resize; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); }
  .handle::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 7px; top: 35%; bottom: 35%; width: 4px; border-left: 2px solid rgba(11, 34, 48, 0.55); border-right: 2px solid rgba(11, 34, 48, 0.55); box-sizing: border-box; }
  .handle:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--pink); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .trim { margin: 0; font: 500 14px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .trim strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px 16px; }
  .controls label { display: grid; gap: 4px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
  .controls select { font: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-size: 15px; padding: 8px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); }

  .size { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 6px 12px; }
  .size strong { font: 700 34px/1 var(--display); }
  .size span { font: 400 13px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .fits { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .fits :global(li) { font: 600 14px/1 var(--body); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 999px; }
  .fits :global(.ok) { background: #DDF5EA; color: #11795A; }
  .fits :global(.no) { background: #FDE3EA; color: #B4234F; }
  .fits :global(.wait) { background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .tip { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 0; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: #FFF4D6; color: #6B4E00; font-size: 15px; }
  .tip button { font: 600 14px/1 var(--body); padding: 9px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: #6B4E00; color: #FFF4D6; cursor: pointer; }

  .buttons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .btn { font: 600 16px/1 var(--body); padding: 15px 22px; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; }
  .btn.primary { border: 0; background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); }
  .btn.primary:hover { background: #047FAB; }
  .btn.primary[aria-disabled='true'] { opacity: 0.5; pointer-events: none; }
  .btn.ghost { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); }
  .btn.ghost:hover { background: var(--wash); }
  .btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
  .alt { display: grid; gap: 10px; padding: 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--wash); }
  .alt p { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .alt p strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .alt-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px 14px; }
  .alt-row .btn { font-size: 15px; padding: 11px 16px; }
  .alt-row :global(a) { font-weight: 600; color: var(--sky); }
  .bug { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .bug a { color: var(--sky); font-weight: 600; }
  .reset { justify-self: start; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .panes { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
